sequenceDiagram
    actor "Client" as Client
    participant "Presentation Layer" as PresentationLayer
    participant "Application Layer" as ApplicationLayer
    participant "Infrastructure Layer" as InfrastructureLayer
    participant "Database" as Database
    participant "Logging & Monitoring" as LoggingMonitoring

    activate PresentationLayer
    Client->>PresentationLayer: 1. POST /api/v1/library/items/{itemId}/complete
    PresentationLayer-->>Client: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error with JSON body: {"error":"An unexpected error occurred.","correlationId":"..."}
    activate ApplicationLayer
    PresentationLayer->>ApplicationLayer: 2. Dispatch(new CompleteBookCommand(itemId, userId))
    ApplicationLayer-->>PresentationLayer: Throws DbUpdateException
    activate InfrastructureLayer
    ApplicationLayer->>InfrastructureLayer: 3. Begin Database Transaction
    InfrastructureLayer-->>ApplicationLayer: Transaction context established
    ApplicationLayer->>InfrastructureLayer: 4. Update LibraryItem status to 'Read' in DbContext
    activate Database
    InfrastructureLayer->>Database: 5. EXEC SQL: UPDATE "LibraryItems" SET ...
    Database-->>InfrastructureLayer: Success (Rows affected: 1)
    ApplicationLayer->>InfrastructureLayer: 6. Update Goal progress in DbContext (causes violation)
    InfrastructureLayer->>InfrastructureLayer: 7. Execute DbContext.SaveChangesAsync()
    InfrastructureLayer-->>InfrastructureLayer: Throws DbUpdateException
    InfrastructureLayer->>Database: 7.1. EXEC SQL: UPDATE "Goals" SET ...
    Database-->>InfrastructureLayer: [ERROR: 23505 unique_violation]
    Database->>InfrastructureLayer: 7.2. Return database error
    ApplicationLayer->>PresentationLayer: 8. Exception propagates to Global Exception Handling Middleware
    PresentationLayer->>InfrastructureLayer: 9. Trigger Transaction Rollback (via DbContext.Dispose())
    InfrastructureLayer->>Database: 10. EXEC SQL: ROLLBACK TRANSACTION
    Database-->>InfrastructureLayer: Success
    activate LoggingMonitoring
    PresentationLayer->>LoggingMonitoring: 11. Log Critical Error

    note over InfrastructureLayer: CRITICAL: The rollback is an automatic side effect of the DbContext being disposed while its tran...
    note over PresentationLayer: The global exception middleware is configured in Program.cs and acts as a centralized, top-level ...

    deactivate LoggingMonitoring
    deactivate Database
    deactivate InfrastructureLayer
    deactivate ApplicationLayer
    deactivate PresentationLayer
